hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21454","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Ajlah: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza narrated to us from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to present the Quran to you. He said: And did my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, name me to you. He said: By the favor of Allah and by His mercy, so in that let them rejoice. Thus Ubayy recited it."
"21455","Muammal narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Aslam al-Minqari narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ubayy, I was commanded to recite to you such and such a surah. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and was I mentioned there. He said: Yes. So I said to him: O Abu al-Mundhir, did you rejoice at that. He said: And what prevents me, while Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Say, by the favor of Allah and by His mercy, so in that let them rejoice, it is better than what they gather. Muammal said: I said to Sufyan: Is this recitation in the hadith. He said: Yes."
"21456","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me: Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not revile the wind, so when you see of it what you dislike, say: O Allah, we ask You of the good of this wind and the good of what is in it and the good of what it was sent with, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this wind and the evil of what is in it and the evil of what it was sent with."
"21457","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Kufi narrated to us: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Dharr ibn Abdullah from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the wind, for it is from the relief of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and ask Allah its good and the good of what is in it and the good of what it was sent with, and seek refuge in Allah from its evil and the evil of what is in it and the evil of what it was sent with."
"21458","Abdullah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us from Sufyan from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Dharr from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr and omitted a verse, so Ubayy came having missed part of the prayer, and when he finished he said: O Messenger of Allah, was this verse abrogated or were you made to forget it. He said: No, rather I was made to forget it."
"21459","Abdullah narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us from al-Amash from Talhah and Zubayd from Dharr from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Say, O you disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One."
"21460","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us: my father narrated to us from al-Amash from Talhah al-Yami from Dharr from Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: Say, O you disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One, and when he gave salam he said: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy, three times."
"21461","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Bazzaz narrated to me: Abu Umar al-Darir al-Basri narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us from Zubayd from Dharr from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"21462","Abdullah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to me: my father narrated to me from his father from Salamah from Saeed ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us when we woke in the morning: We woke upon the fitrah of Islam and the word of sincerity and the sunnah of our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the religion of our father Ibrahim, upright, Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists, and when we evening likewise."
"21463","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Habib ibn al-Zubayr who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl hear Ibn Abza hear Abdullah ibn Khabbab hear Ubayy narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: One of his eyes is as if a green glass, and seek refuge in Allah, Blessed and Exalted, from the torment of the grave."
"21464","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Habib ibn al-Zubayr who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl hear Ibn Abza hear Abdullah ibn Khabbab hear Ubayy narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: One of his eyes is as if a green glass, and seek refuge in Allah, Blessed and Exalted, from the torment of the grave."
"21465","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Habib ibn al-Zubayr from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from Abdullah ibn Khabbab from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Dajjal, and he mentioned similar to it."
"21466","Abdullah narrated to us: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Shubah informed us: Habib ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it, and Khallad did not mention in his hadith Abdullah ibn Khabbab."
